# =============================================================================
# Morphic-G AOS — Credential & Key Reference
# =============================================================================
#
# This project does NOT use a .env file at runtime.
# This file is a reference guide only — showing every credential, token, and
# key the system needs, where it lives, and how it gets there.
#
# DO NOT create a real .env file with actual values.
# DO NOT set GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS — it breaks ADC silently.
#
# Legend:
#   [ADC]            Handled automatically by Application Default Credentials
#   [settings.yaml]  Goes in config/settings.yaml (gitignored)
#   [Secret Manager] Stored in GCP Secret Manager, fetched at agent boot
#   [local file]     Lives on disk only, gitignored
#   [GCP Console]    Configured in the GCP web console, not in files
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE CLOUD AUTHENTICATION
# Handled by ADC — no value needed in any file
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local dev:  run once — gcloud auth application-default login --client-id-file=oauth-client.json ...
# Cloud Run:  automatically provided by the attached service account identity
# DO NOT SET:
#   GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=   ← leave this unset, always


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GCP PROJECT
# [settings.yaml] config/settings.yaml → gcp.project_id
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GCP_PROJECT_ID=morphic-gaos-prod


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE SHEETS
# [settings.yaml] config/settings.yaml → sheet.workbook_id
#                                       → projects.default.sheet_id
# How to get: URL of the spreadsheet → /spreadsheets/d/<THIS_PART>/edit
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SHEET_WORKBOOK_ID=<your-spreadsheet-id>


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE DRIVE
# [settings.yaml] config/settings.yaml → projects.default.drive_folder_id
# How to get: open the Knowledge/ folder in Drive → URL → /folders/<THIS_PART>
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# DRIVE_KNOWLEDGE_FOLDER_ID=<your-knowledge-folder-id>


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OAUTH DESKTOP CLIENT
# [local file]  oauth-client.json  (gitignored — never commit)
# How to get:   GCP Console → APIs & Services → Credentials
#               → + Create Credentials → OAuth client ID → Desktop app
#               → Download JSON → save as oauth-client.json in repo root
# Used only for local ADC login — not used at runtime
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OAUTH_CLIENT_FILE=oauth-client.json


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI API KEY
# [Secret Manager]  Secret name: GEMINI_API_KEY
# How to get:       GCP Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → + Create Credentials → API key
#                   ⚠️  Must be created in YOUR GCP project (morphic-gaos-prod)
#                       NOT from aistudio.google.com — Studio keys cause 429 quota errors
# How to store:
#   echo -n "AIza..." | gcloud secrets versions add GEMINI_API_KEY --data-file=- --project=morphic-gaos-prod
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OLLAMA HOST
# [Secret Manager]  Secret name: OLLAMA_HOST
# Default value:    http://localhost:11434
# Used for:         Local LLM fallback when Gemini latency/cost is undesirable
# How to store:
#   echo -n "http://localhost:11434" | gcloud secrets versions add OLLAMA_HOST --data-file=- --project=morphic-gaos-prod
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEBHOOK HMAC SECRET
# [Secret Manager]  Secret name: WEBHOOK_HMAC_SECRET
# What it is:       32-byte random hex string — signs and verifies webhook payloads
#                   between the Apps Script and Nexus-Prime
# How to generate:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# How to store:
#   echo -n "<hex-value>" | gcloud secrets versions add WEBHOOK_HMAC_SECRET --data-file=- --project=morphic-gaos-prod
# Also copy the same value into Apps Script → Project Settings → Script Properties
#   Key: WEBHOOK_HMAC_SECRET
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# WEBHOOK_HMAC_SECRET=<32-byte hex string>


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEBHOOK URL
# [Secret Manager]  Secret name: WEBHOOK_URL
# What it is:       The deployed Apps Script Web App URL
# When to add:      After §4.7 of the Deploy Spec (Apps Script → Deploy → New deployment)
# How to store:
#   echo -n "https://script.google.com/macros/s/.../exec" | \
#     gcloud secrets versions add WEBHOOK_URL --data-file=- --project=morphic-gaos-prod
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# WEBHOOK_URL=https://script.google.com/macros/s/.../exec


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BIGQUERY
# No credentials needed — BigQuery client uses ADC automatically
# Dataset and tables created via bq CLI in §7 of the Deploy Spec
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUB/SUB
# No credentials needed — Pub/Sub client uses ADC automatically
# Topics created via gcloud CLI in §5 of the Deploy Spec
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERTEX AI / MEMORY BANK
# No credentials needed — Vertex AI client uses ADC automatically
# Corpus resource names stored in config/settings.yaml → memory_bank.corpora
# Populated after §12 of the Deploy Spec
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
